6. Technical Uncertainties & Honest Assessment
While these four domains represent frontier capabilities, practical engineering faces several critical constraints:


* Quantum Advantage in Machine Learning: Current NISQ devices suffer from hardware decoherence, gate infidelities, and the theoretical challenge of "barren plateaus" (exponential vanishing gradients in randomly initialized circuits). Empirical quantum advantage over classical deep learning has not yet been demonstrated on real-world industrial benchmarks.
* RAG Context Windows vs. In-Context Learning: Massive context LLMs (1M+ tokens) reduce the necessity for chunking in small document sets, but empirical studies reveal performance degradation ("needle-in-a-haystack" retrieval dropoffs) compared to targeted hybrid RAG.
* Multi-Agent Convergence & Tool Drift: Autonomous agent swarms are prone to cascading error compounding, infinite reasoning loops, and unpredictable latency. Production reliability requires strict state machines and bounded retries rather than unconstrained autonomy.
* Fine-Tuning Catastrophic Forgetting: Parameter-efficient fine-tuning (QLoRA) preserves general conversational ability better than full fine-tuning, but specialized domain training can still degrade broader multi-task reasoning without balanced replay datasets.


